        </profile>
        <profile name="The Ammunition Sacrement" id="a4d6-37b4-32e3-3cde" hidden="false" typeId="058c-866b-6487-ccc4" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="2ecd-b4ff-9e78-a8e2">Ammunition Sacrament ACTION: A Mendelist Ammo Monk can take an Ammunition Sacrament ACTION. If they do so, take a Risky Success Roll for the Mendelist Ammo Monk. If the roll is a Failure, the Mendelist Ammo Monk’s Activation ends. If the roll is a Success or a Critical Success, pick 1 friendly model within 1&quot; of the Mendelist Ammo Monk and in their Line of Sight, and then pick one of the following Ammunition Sacraments. The Sacrament you pick applies to the model until the end of its next Activation.


* Bullet of the Guided Path Sacrament: Add +1 DICE to rolls for Ranged Attacks made by the model.
* Cartridge of his Wrath Sacrament: Add the BLAST 2&quot; and SHRAPNEL Keywords to Ranged Weapons used by the model that do not have the BLAST or FLAMETHROWER Keywords.
* Echo of his Word Sacrament: Add +1 INJURY DICE to rolls for Ranged Attacks made by the model .</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Faithful Followers" id="d1bd-c32a-6365-587a" hidden="false" typeId="058c-866b-6487-ccc4" typeName="Ability">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="2ecd-b4ff-9e78-a8e2">When you Activate a model within 1&quot; of a Mendelist Ammo Monk, you can also Activate the Mendelist Monk if they have not yet been Activated during the Turn. If you do so, the two models can take their ACTIONS in any order you wish, and you can switch between the two models freely. If the Activation of either model ends (due to a failed Risky Success Roll, for example), the other model can carry on with its Activation normally.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
